.\" uustat.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX uustat(1) utility, which
.\" this tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/UUSTAT.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/UUSTAT.
.TH UUSTAT 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
uustat \- uucp status inquiry and job control
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Uustat
is not provided on maux.
none of this exists on maux: there is no printer, no mail
transport, and no UUCP.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tip(1)
